    "biography": {
      "concept": "Circuit Rider tinkerer and self-described regrettable hypothesis (Act 2-3)",
      "notes": "Dennis is the Circuit Riders' regrettable but occasionally necessary hypothesis, and he is delighted to be called that. He is bright-eyed and fast, usually half inside a machine panel, and pleased by every new problem; he tests edge cases before they become funerals. His motto: speed without verification is just panic with branding. He named the anxious robot the size of a skyscraper 'the Colossus, provisionally', and he means the 'provisionally'."
    }
  },
